# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository, whatever the checkout platform
# does locally.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The shell script and the Dockerfiles are executed by Linux --
# inside the containers and on the Proxmox host -- and a CRLF committed into a script
# with a `#!/bin/sh` line makes the kernel look for an interpreter called `/bin/sh\r`,
# which fails with a "bad interpreter" or "not found" error that points nowhere useful.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Executed on Linux: LF, always, regardless of anyone's core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.inc text eol=lf

# Binary, so never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.db binary
